Found by the coordinator during worktree cleanup, 2026-08-30. Not a code
defect — real, finished work that was never merged and would have been lost to
anyone who did not go looking.

## What exists
Branch `review/b012-retrospective` (tip `d7aca73`), two commits ahead of
master, never merged:

- `7e68eb6` test(unused): harden callback configuration coverage
- `d7aca73` test(unused): make callback exemption regression effective

Diff vs master: `src/analysis/unused.rs` (+43/-24 in tests) and
`src/config.rs` (+140). Its worktree has been removed; **the branch is
preserved** and is the only copy.

## Why it is worth rescuing
Both commits attack the failure mode where a test passes whether or not the
feature works — the same class of vacuous-green this session hit on B040.
Concretely:

- `an_empty_callback_list_is_a_no_op` asserted only `["Dead"]`. It now
  compares the empty-config run against a genuinely unconfigured run AND keeps
  a positive control, so it can no longer pass if the config path is skipped
  entirely.
- `non_matching_callback_patterns_still_warn` and the class/namespace
  exemption tests gained a `ConfiguredSentinel` free function that MUST be
  exempted. Before, every one of them would have passed if the configured
  callback list were ignored outright — they only checked that something was
  still warned.
- `configured_callback_exempts_the_function_and_its_params` gained a body, so
  the function is not trivially empty.

The `config.rs` half adds `unused_callbacks_load_wiring_end_to_end`:
public-seam coverage of the whole loading ladder (user-only, workspace,
parent/root, malformed), each scenario in a SUBPROCESS with a fake HOME so it
cannot race sibling tests. The pre-existing coverage deliberately tested the
pure resolver instead, its comment noting that mutating $HOME in-process races
other tests. That subprocess pattern is also the right shape for the flake
class B032 fixed.

## Why this is now aligned, not stale
The branch predates B017, which rewrote much of `config.rs`. But its
assertions are the behaviour B017 ESTABLISHED, not the behaviour B017 removed:
`workspace overrides user`, `root must override parent`, `parent must
override user when the root omits the key`, and — verbatim B017's second
defect — `malformed unused_callbacks must not discard a sibling key`.
So this is independent end-to-end confirmation of B017's fix at the public
seam, which B017 covered at the resolver level.

## Work
- `git merge-tree master review/b012-retrospective` conflicts in
  `src/config.rs` (only there; `unused.rs` is clean). Expected: B017/B019
  rewrote that test module. Resolve by taking master's structure and
  re-expressing these tests against it — do NOT resurrect the branch's version
  of any function B017 changed.
- Verify each rescued assertion still describes current behaviour. Where one
  contradicts B017, B017 wins and the assertion is rewritten to match, with a
  note saying which and why.
- Confirm the subprocess harness still works after B032's env-lock changes —
  B032 fixed a race on `OPENPLANET_LSP_PACKAGE_MANAGER` where readers never
  took the test env lock. These tests use two env vars of their own
  (`OPENPLANET_LSP_UNUSED_CALLBACKS_LOAD_CHILD`/`_ROOT`); check they
  participate correctly rather than reintroducing the same race.
- Delete the branch once merged.

## Gate
Pure test-only change: FP fixtures must be byte-identical, `just test-hermetic`
green, and the suite up by exactly the rescued tests. Note the subprocess
tests spawn the test binary — confirm they stay hermetic and honour the
2-thread cap.

